# Small-company lobbying-jump re-check

Rule tested: quarter-over-quarter top-10 lobbying jumps, only companies worth under $2B on the signal day, bought on the first trading day on/after the signal day, held 252 trading days, equal weight across whatever is held each day.
Baseline: IWM (small-company index fund), measured on exactly the same days. SPY is measured on exactly the same days.
Versions looked at before choosing this slice: 16. Because of that, the 'not luck' bar is t >= 2.95, not 2.
No bet sizing is used. If this is ever traded, size at half-Kelly or less, never full Kelly.

